  "term": "impulsion",
  "definition": "Impulsion is a drive or striving that acts by its own force rather than as part of a person's wider organized thinking and aims. It refers to action pushed forward by the immediate strength of a tendency, in contrast with action shaped by reflection and deliberation.",
